    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "Registering `GET /a` twice, or `GET /a` and a `MethodSet` registration containing `GET` on `/a`, makes the freeze raise a configuration error. [D-056]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 853
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "Registering `GET /a/:x` and `GET /a/:y` makes the freeze raise a configuration error, while `GET /a/:x` and `POST /a/:y` freeze without error. [D-057]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 854
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "The configuration error message names the method and the pattern of both conflicting registrations, and registration itself does not raise it before the freeze. [D-058] [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-2-2 SDS-AC-12] The freeze throws one `RoutingConfigException` whose message has one line per conflicting pair, \"METHOD pattern conflicts with METHOD pattern\".",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 855
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "With case-insensitive matching on, `GET /Users` and `GET /users` conflict at freeze; with trailing-slash ignoring on, `GET /a` and `GET /a/` conflict; under the strict default neither pair conflicts. [loop W residual: normalised conflicts] Case-insensitive conflict keys use the same Unicode code-point folding as runtime literal/prefix matching, including supplementary characters.",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 856
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "Registering a `TRACE` route while `TRACE` routing is disabled makes the freeze raise a configuration error, and likewise for `CONNECT`; a WebSocket registration and a `GET` registration on the same pattern freeze without error. [loop W residual; D-068] [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-2-2 SDS-AC-14] The freeze error line reads \"METHOD pattern registered while METHOD routing is disabled\".",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 857
      }
    ],
