    "requirement": "The system shall provide a route-table freeze, which wave 4 calls inside `listen()` before any socket is bound, that raises a configuration error naming both conflicting registrations when two registrations of the same route kind share a method and have the same pattern or patterns that differ only in variable names, comparing patterns normalised under the active path-form policies, and when a `TRACE` or `CONNECT` route is registered while that method's routing is disabled.",
    "rationale": "Covers D-056, D-057, D-058 (T03) and the loop W residual (conflict detection on policy-normalised patterns; a TRACE or CONNECT route while disabled is a configuration error at freeze). A WebSocket route and a `GET` route on one pattern do not conflict (D-068).",
